# wip — vscode-workspace-atlas
# Branch: feature/vscode-workspace-atlas
# Started: 2026-03-26

#:layer #!pragmatics

^["intent"]{
 ~#goal: "Add a workspace atlas view that renders roots, memory tiers, generated surfaces, and harness locations from the workspace contract."
 ~#taste: "clarity, layering, naming"
}

^["stream"]{
 >>[2026-03-26 00:00] observe — the extension currently exposes one Concepts tree and a hardcoded root map while `.spw/workspace.spw` already defines a richer discovery contract.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:01] decide — the atlas should read as a workspace map first and a file browser second; roots, planes, and memory ownership should be explicit.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:02] observe — the workspace manifest already names future LSP/editor capabilities, which makes it a natural source for view vocabulary and command naming.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:03] hygiene — base reference recorded at `main@f42a80fa8eefb813992e21f7461c96926f033416`; `main...HEAD` shows no unrelated committed drift.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:04] hygiene — local drift is present in `extensions/vscode-spw/src/annotation-index.ts`, `extensions/vscode-spw/src/extension.ts`, and `packages/spw-lsp/src/stdio-server.ts`; feature implementation should isolate that work before commit 1.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:05] taste — the atlas should reinforce the workspace's own nouns instead of adding editor-only taxonomy.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:06] revise — expand the atlas spec to include cross-tree resonance, graph-query affordances, and rotation between topology, contract, and query perspectives.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:07] observe — the three vscode plans (atlas, register-explorer, authoring-probe-loop) form one river (where am I → what is alive → what can I do) but lack a shared interaction model; each plan wires into extension.ts and context.ts independently.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:08] decide — create vscode-interaction-contract.spw as a cross-plan artifact defining shared event vocabulary, SpwContext evolution, and merge sequencing. Atlas lands first, establishes manifestState + workspaceTemperature + activeRoot.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:09] observe — spirit sequence (?~@&*^) is declared in SIGIL_SEMANTICS and manifest but not experientially present in any plan. The atlas should make phase a navigable axis, not just metadata.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:10] decide — add phase as a fifth rotation perspective alongside topology, contract, resonance, query. Compute dominant phase per node via operator frequency analysis. This mirrors the manifest's own `$%[op.distribution]` probe.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:11] observe — materialization cycle (priming → concept → frame → body) is declared in manifest ^"priming_concepts_frames_bodies" but absent from all three plans. Each stage has different inspection affordances.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:12] decide — atlas nodes carry materialization badges. Heuristic: scan for ~bindings, ^frames, and ProjectionEntry presence. Stale bodies are "ungrounded."
 >>[2026-03-26 00:13] observe — Memory section was planned as static labels (hot/warm/cold/generated). But ServerIndex already tracks live cache tiers with beat age and mutation.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:14] decide — Memory shows two layers: declared placement (manifest) and observed temperature (index). LSP exposes spw/workspaceTemperature request.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:15] observe — resonance is mentioned throughout the plans but never computationally defined. Four channels exist in the LSP: annotation co-occurrence, root cross-reference, projection lineage, register coupling.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:16] decide — define resonance as the union of four channels. LSP exposes spw/resonance endpoint. Atlas "Show Resonance Neighbors" queries all four, strongest channel first.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:17] resolve — answer ?[manifest_authority] with authority table: structural claims from manifest, behavioral observations from index. When manifest absent, inferred data is labeled clearly.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:18] taste — command names should use Spw vocabulary: Re-ground over Refresh, Unprimed over Not initialized, Ungrounded over Stale. The extension teaches the language by speaking it.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:19] revise — relax the three-plan contract from fixed merge order to additive capability composition. Atlas still provides the shared substrate, but all three surfaces now need solo-ship and pairwise-integration stories.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:20] observe — the interaction contract defines seven events but doesn't distinguish extension-internal events (vscode.EventEmitter, synchronous) from LSP-bridged requests (process boundary, async). These are different transports with different cost profiles.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:21] decide — add ^["transport"] frame classifying each event. All seven UI events are extension-internal. Five LSP requests (spw/resonance, spw/workspaceTemperature, spw/registerSnapshot, spw/operatorFrequency, spw/phaseContext) cross the process boundary.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:22] observe — SpwContext capability checks are described but the implementation pattern isn't specified. Optional fields (T | null) vs branded capability interfaces.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:23] decide — use optional fields (T | null) as the simplest additive pattern. Consuming code checks `if (spw.manifestState)` before accessing. Branded interfaces can be added later if type narrowing becomes noisy.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:24] observe — stdio-server.ts is 900+ lines and three plans each add new LSP handlers. Piling dispatch into one file creates a merge bottleneck.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:25] decide — add ^["handler_registration"] frame. Substrate commit extracts handler registration from stdio-server.ts before surface plans add new handlers.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:26] observe — two things called "phase" across plans: spirit-sequence phase (?~@&*^) describes operator semantics; register pipeline phase (lex, parse, semantic, optimize, pragmatic) describes when runtime enriched a register. These are orthogonal axes, not synonyms.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:27] decide — add ^["phase_vocabularies"] frame reconciling the two axes. Atlas/authoring use "phase" = spirit-sequence. Register explorer uses "phase" = pipeline. Detail views show both when both are available.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:28] observe — VS Code plans have no cross-theme dependency annotations. runtime-telemetry-canon provides the data for resonance channel 4 and rich register snapshots. register-phase-evolution provides canonical pipeline-phase vocabulary. absorb-spwq-cli provides reliable selector traversal. monorepo-workspace-foundation may shift import paths.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:29] decide — add ^["cross_theme_enrichments"] frame listing runtime/parser plans as enrichment providers with solo-ship fallbacks. Add cross-theme enrichment subsections to all three VS Code plan Dependencies.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:30] observe — authoring loop's look-back rule needs a cursor-offset-to-phase-context query from the seed parser. Not currently scoped in any plan.
 >>[2026-03-26 00:31] decide — note seed_phase_context as an unscoped enrichment in the interaction contract. Flag register-phase-evolution as the natural home for this addition (adjacent to selector-expression grammar work).
}

^["open"]{
 ?[cross_surface_temperature]: "Should the atlas's live temperature view include documents from roots the manifest doesn't declare, or only manifest-scoped files?"
 ?[phase_computation_cost]: "Operator frequency analysis per root on every refresh may be expensive for large workspaces. Should phase badges be computed lazily (on expand) or cached with beat-based invalidation?"
}

^["resolved"]{
 ![manifest_authority]: {
  ~#answer: "Structural claims come from the manifest; behavioral observations come from the index."
  ~#rule: "When manifest is absent, inferred data is labeled 'inferred' and never presented as canonical."
  ~#table: "Roots=manifest-strict (fallback: ROOT_MAP labeled inferred), Memory=manifest placement + index temperature (fallback: index only), Generated=manifest spec owners + index stale (fallback: hide), Harness=manifest-strict (fallback: hide), Contracts=manifest-strict (fallback: hide), Queries=index-derived manifest-scoped (fallback: discovered files only)"
  ~#resolved_at: "2026-03-26 00:17"
 }
}

